/bin/bash -lc "cat > .impeccable/surface.md <<'EOF'
# Studio surface

Mode: Operate. Code-led, inferred under the user's explicit no-interview instruction.

## Grounded worlds
1. Polish mathematical publishing: clear diagrams and neutral text.
2. School geometry sets: measured alignment and compact labels.
3. Botanical identification guides: branching programs with green ink.
4. Public library learning spaces: calm navigation and open work areas.
5. Children's construction paper: discrete geometric colour roles.
6. Geometric educational print: pine ink, chalk paper, graph fields and dense but readable worked examples.
7. Museum science workshops: independent stations and direct manipulation.

The category rut is a terminal costume or a dashboard of feature cards. Candidate 6 is the assigned world. Challengers: transit diagram declined (route topology obscures editing; retain contextual orientation); metro declined (oversized type hurts source density; retain decisive selection); star atlas competitive in identification, weaker task clarity; cassette declined (physical flip obscures simultaneous source/drawing; retain persistent position); event catalog declined (thumbnail density competes with source; retain genuine example previews); data sublime declined (pure monochrome loses stroke semantics; retain precise alignment).

## Direction contract
THESIS: A learner sees editable instructions and their geometric consequence together, with familiar studio controls.
OWN-WORLD: Restrained pine/green shell, chalk drawing field, graphite source and copper secondary drawing ink. System sans for UI, monospace only for code and coordinates. Compact rectangular controls with consistent soft corners.
STORY: Open a working rosette, run or step it, discover examples, inspect a command and make a drawing to share. Source and drawing remain the principal work areas.
FIRST VIEWPORT: A dark pine header holds brand and four standard navigation choices. A slim title row precedes a split editor/drawing studio, 40/60 on desktop. Execution buttons and speed sit above source; camera controls sit above the canvas. The signature move is synchronized line-to-stroke stepping: a green source line and the oriented turtle visibly locate the current operation. A compact row of actual example previews follows the studio.
FORM: Grounded world 6, geometric educational print; seed:ac0633560b7629fe. Narrow screens stack source and drawing, retaining all controls. Motion conveys execution and camera manipulation only; reduced motion disables decorative transitions.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance
EOF
